{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.10"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":8831173}],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":5,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"id":"d6928af6-17da-430a-9762-6c6ddf79068d","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Real-Time Lightweight Deepfake Audio Detection using Tiny SSL + Lightweight CNN\n\n**BTP (B.Tech Project) — Research Notebook**\n\n### Objective\nThis notebook implements and trains a **binary audio deepfake detector** (Real vs. Fake / Bonafide vs. Spoof)\non the **ASVspoof2024** dataset, designed to be **lightweight enough for real-time / edge deployment**.\n\n### Architecture\n\n```\nInput Audio\n    │\n    ▼\nVoice Activity Detection (VAD)\n    │\n    ▼\nLog-Mel Spectrogram (80-dim)\n    │\n    ▼\nTiny SSL Encoder (DistilHuBERT)\n    │\n    ▼\nLightweight CNN (MobileNetV3-Small / EfficientNet-Lite0)\n    │\n    ▼\nWavelet Block (optional, PyWavelets DWT fusion)\n    │\n    ▼\nSelf-Attention Pooling\n    │\n    ▼\nClassifier Head (Linear → Dropout → GELU → Linear)\n    │\n    ▼\nReal / Fake\n```\n\n### Key Design Goals\n1. **Low latency / low parameter count** — suitable for real-time inference on commodity or edge hardware.\n2. **Self-supervised speech representations** distilled into a tiny encoder (DistilHuBERT) to retain\n   robust phonetic/prosodic cues used by SOTA anti-spoofing systems, without the cost of full HuBERT/Wav2Vec2.\n3. **CNN backbone reuse** (MobileNetV3-Small / EfficientNet-Lite0) treats the SSL feature sequence as a\n   2D \"image\" to exploit efficient, well-optimized vision architectures for local artifact detection.\n4. **Optional wavelet-domain fusion** to capture multi-resolution spectral artifacts characteristic of\n   vocoder-based synthesis (a known deepfake signature).\n5. **Attention pooling** for a variable-length-robust, discriminative utterance-level embedding.\n\n### Dataset\n**ASVspoof 2024 (LA/DF track)** — bonafide vs. spoofed speech utterances with official train/dev/eval\nprotocol files.\n\n### Reproducibility\nAll experiments use a fixed random seed, deterministic data splits (as defined by ASVspoof protocol files),\nand full configuration logging (see `CONFIG` in Cell 5).\n\n---\n*Framework: PyTorch, torchaudio, HuggingFace Transformers, torchvision, timm, PyWavelets, librosa, scikit-learn.*","metadata":{}},{"id":"98d86543-1e02-46af-8446-a2663868c596","cell_type":"code","source":"# ==============================================================\n# Cell 2: Install dependencies\n# ==============================================================\n# Run this once. In Colab/Kaggle/local Jupyter with internet access.\n# Comment out lines for packages you already have installed.\n\n%pip install -q torch torchaudio --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121\n%pip install -q torchvision\n%pip install -q transformers>=4.40.0\n%pip install -q timm\n%pip install -q librosa\n%pip install -q PyWavelets\n%pip install -q scikit-learn\n%pip install -q pandas numpy matplotlib tqdm\n%pip install -q soundfile\n%pip install -q onnx onnxruntime\n# Optional (only needed if you want WebRTC-based VAD instead of the built-in energy-based VAD):\n%pip install -q webrtcvad","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-14T17:33:43.588482Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-14T17:33:43.588741Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-14T17:34:25.254372Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-14T17:33:43.588721Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-14T17:34:25.253409Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Note: you may need to restart the kernel to use updated packages.\nNote: you may need to restart the kernel to use updated packages.\nNote: you may need to restart the kernel to use updated packages.\nNote: you may need to restart the kernel to use